{"title":"Dwarkesh’s Question","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/912665402/0/marginalrevolution~Dwarkeshs-Question.html","date":1739189585000,"content":"<blockquote><p>One question I had for you while we were talking about the intelligence stuff was, as a scientist yourself, what do you make of the fact that these things have basically the entire corpus of human knowledge memorized and they haven’t been able to make a single new connection that has led to a discovery? Whereas if even a moderately intelligent person had this much stuff memorized, they would notice — Oh, this thing causes this symptom. This other thing also causes this symptom. There’s a medical cure right here.</p>\r\n<p>Shouldn’t we be expecting that kind of stuff?</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>It’s a very good question. In 2023, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/ATabarrok/status/1727039127575843288\">I quipped</a>, “I think they have, we just haven’t asked them.” Maybe, but less clear today. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/1888164523984470055\">Dwarkesh reports</a> that there have been no good answers.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/02/dwarkeshs-question.html\">Dwarkesh’s Question</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/912665402/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/912665402/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/912665402/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/912665402/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/19/912665402/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/email20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/20/912665402/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/rss20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/02/dwarkeshs-question.html#comments\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/comments20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/02/dwarkeshs-question.html/feed\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/commentsrss20.png\" /></a> \r\n<div><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/02/dwarkeshs-question.html#comments\"><h3>Comments</h3></a><ul><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/02/dwarkeshs-question.html#comment-160873143\">In my experience, LLMs don't make great original value ...</a> <i>by Bill</i></li><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/02/dwarkeshs-question.html#comment-160873098\">In reply to Dinwar.   &gt; Never mind that LLMs work with words ...</a> <i>by PHinton</i></li><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/02/dwarkeshs-question.html#comment-160873077\">In reply to Old Programmer.   Can curiosity be prompted?</a> <i>by bazza</i></li><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/02/dwarkeshs-question.html#comment-160873074\">I deeply value the willingness to acknowledge mistakes, and I ...</a> <i>by Saturn</i></li><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/02/dwarkeshs-question.html#comment-160873058\">In reply to OldCurmudegon.   I think you are right. Take MD, ...</a> <i>by Floccina</i></li><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/02/dw